        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Plants: Hibiscus waimeae, H. arnottianus, Hawaiian hibiscus\n- Places: Oʻahu, Molokaʻi, Hawaii\n- Concepts: native species, flower color, habitat, elevation\n\nFacts:\n- Hawaiian hibiscus are seven species of hibiscus regarded as native to Hawaii.\n- H. arnottianus of Oʻahu and Molokaʻi and H. waimeae are the only Hawaiian hibiscuses that have white flowers.\n- H. waimeae inhabits coastal mesic, mixed mesic, and wet forests at elevations of 250 meters and above.",
